    "id": "1780468090934",
    "title": "This is second note",
    "content": "## Behavioral framing\n\nThe core behavior under test is **continuous work with voluntary quiescence**:\n\n- an LLM agent works continuously while it has a live task,\n- when a unit of work completes, it voluntarily enters a waiting state,\n- it remains ready for expected or unexpected stimulus,\n- and it resumes cleanly when the runtime, avatar, or environment issues the next trigger.\n\nThis makes the benchmark about more than task completion. It is also about whether the runtime can preserve cooperative waiting, restore the agent correctly, and make those transitions visible in telemetry.\n\nThere are two useful variants:",
